@SocialNetworkPlatformProject_HostAddress = http://localhost:5051

# Try the API from Visual Studio: send "login" first, the other requests reuse its token.
# (Swagger at /swagger lists every endpoint; this file is only a few quick examples.)

### Is the server up and the database answering? (200 "Healthy")
GET {{SocialNetworkPlatformProject_HostAddress}}/health

### Sign in
# @name login
POST {{SocialNetworkPlatformProject_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "emailOrUserName": "you@example.com",
  "password": "your password"
}

### My news feed
GET {{SocialNetworkPlatformProject_HostAddress}}/api/posts/feed
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### The devices my account is signed in on
GET {{SocialNetworkPlatformProject_HostAddress}}/api/auth/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### My notifications
GET {{SocialNetworkPlatformProject_HostAddress}}/api/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
